Prior art
---------
keelyard's output filters, structure-first reading and usage report were designed after
studying the following projects. No source code from them is included in keelyard; the
implementations here are written from scratch in Python. They are credited because their
ideas shaped this work:

- rtk (https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk), Apache-2.0: per-command output filtering,
  grouping, deduplication, and recalling elided output by content hash.
- repomix (https://github.com/yamadashy/repomix), MIT: compressing code to its structure
  before handing it to a model.
- claude-context-optimizer (https://github.com/AzozzALFiras/claude-context-optimizer):
  cached reads, function extraction and project maps exposed over MCP.
- ccusage (https://github.com/ccusage/ccusage): reading token usage from Claude Code's
  local session logs.
- tokensave (https://github.com/aovestdipaperino/tokensave), MIT: code-intelligence MCP
  tools for agents.

